SM wrote:
> Hi,
>
> is there an option to set boulder to 0 in Nethack 4? I can't seem to
> find it anywhere. Not a huge problem but as I'm about to start Sokoban, my
> eye-memory (sic) may cause unexpected trouble: I'm used to 0 and even
> seeing the first Sokoban level with ` as the boulder glyph looks pretty
> intimidating.
>
> Other than this, the game is very playable once you get used to UI and
> little changes here and there. Kudos for the team.

This is basically to do with NitroHack's Unicode engine (which I
haven't got around to changing yet). The unicode symbols used for
everything are customizable via ~/.config/NetHack4/unicode.conf; one
of the customizable symbols is "boulder", and it's "0" by default.
However, if you're playing in the ASCII fallback mode, rather than with
Unicode, it just uses the default symbols specified by vanilla, with no
currently implemented way to change them. You're not the only person
with this problem, so I guess it's a case of "patches are welcome" for
the time being. I'm hoping to rewrite the relevant code someday, but I'm
busy with real life stuff at the moment and there are also lots of other
things that need changing.

